cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KARA in research, teaching or a publication, please cite it as follows."
title: "KARA — a tiny declarative reactive language for desktop UI prototyping"
abstract: >-
  KARA is a language and runtime for prototyping reactive desktop UIs. It ships a
  complete compiler pipeline (lexer, parser, semantic analysis, static type
  inference, component expansion), a zero-dependency tree-walker interpreter with
  a reactive dependency graph, a language server (LSP) with live diagnostics and
  completion, a Tauri desktop shell, and a fully client-side browser playground.
type: software
